hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27828","Rawh and Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, they said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Ma'qil al-Asadiyyah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend Hajj but my camel is lean, so what do you command me? He said: Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"27829","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, he said: Marwan sent to Umm Ma'qil al-Asadiyyah asking her about this hadith, so she narrated to him that her husband had dedicated a young camel of hers for the sake of Allah, and that she wanted to perform Umrah, so she asked her husband for the young camel and he refused, so she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so he commanded him to give it to her. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hajj and Umrah are of the path of Allah. And he said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj, or suffices as a Hajj. And Hajjaj said: Equals a Hajj, or suffices as a Hajj."
"27830","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi, from Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil, that his mother came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said, and he mentioned its meaning."
"27831","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abu Ma'qil, from Umm Ma'qil, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"27832","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, he said: I was among those who rode with Marwan when he rode to Umm Ma'qil. He said: And I was among those of the people who entered upon her with him, and I heard her when she narrated this hadith."
"27833","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Ma'qil ibn Umm Ma'qil al-Asadiyyah, from Umm Ma'qil al-Asadiyyah, she said: I intended Hajj with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Awza'i from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir."
"27834","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abu Ma'qil, from Umm Ma'qil, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"27835","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari informed me, from Abu Zayd, the freedman of Tha'labah, he informed him, from Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil al-Ansari, among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he narrated to him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade facing the two qiblahs for defecation and urination."
